  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Kings March**: rare: 5 archived performances [5]\n- **Sidekick**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **In Memory of Elizabeth Reed**: rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **Magnificent**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2020-02-16.telefunken-ela-m260.flac2448** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 129 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **soulive2020-02-16.mk4**: source not stated; 13 songs; 128 min [3]\n- **soulive2020-02-16**: source not stated; 13 songs; 128 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: banter/guest, guest [1]\n- Guests: Quinn Sullivan on guitar; a horn section of Brian Thomas, Alex Lee-Clark and Mike Tucker for the rest of the set; Jeffrey Lockhart on guitar [1]\n- Guests included Rahzelle on rap and beatbox, a horn trio of Brian Thomas, Alex Lee-Clark and Mike Tucker, and guitarist Jeffrey Lockhart [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2020-02-16.telefunken-ela-m260.flac2448**: taped by corey the groundhog; transferred by groundhog; source: telefunken ela m260 hypercardioid>v2>r44 [1]. Also: Recorded with a Telefunken ELA M260 hyper cardioid mic through a Lunatec V2 into an Edirol R-44 at 24-bit/48k; Transferred as WAV, run through Audacity, then converted to FLAC with xACT; taped and transferred by corey the groundhog [1]\n- **soulive2020-02-16.mk4**: taped by Bob Hundertmark; transferred by Bob Hundertmark; source: Schoeps MK4->NBox Platinum [3]. Also: Captured with Schoeps MK4 mics (DINA) through NBob Actives and NBox Platinum, with MiAGII Silver Cable, then FLAC [3]\n- **soulive2020-02-16**: taped by J.Cable; transferred by J.Cable; source: AKG ck61's(DIN)>Mixpre6 [2]",
